{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and motion capabilities, separating sensing (uncontrollable) and actuation (controllable) events. The specification encodes a conservative exploration policy: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are used when obstacles are detected. Recovery direction is chosen to avoid oscillation and bias away from blocked sides. Full_rotate is reserved for deadlock recovery only. All states are total on uncontrollables, and only one controllable is enabled per state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion to reflect hardware modularity.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, deterministic exploration with prioritized recovery and steady progress, using helper states for commit and recovery."
  ],
